fact WorkItem(id: "WI-556", description: some(value: "Write an example .anthill demonstrating one/lone integrity constraints (cardinality bound + functional dependency) — the concrete CONSUMER that exercises the WI-020/WI-021 guard optimization. No lone/one constraint exists anywhere in the tree today, so this defines the target SURFACE SHAPE that WI-020's analyze_guard() must recognize. Deliverables: (a) a small domain (e.g. a registry/booking) with at least one cardinality-bound constraint (lone ?x: Sort(...) -: ... = at-most-one) and one functional-dependency (per-key uniqueness) constraint; (b) positive facts that satisfy them + a negative fixture that violates each. DESIGN CRUX to settle jointly with WI-020: a single-level 'lone ?p: Sort(key: ?k) -:' reads as 'at most one matching fact' (CardinalityBound), whereas true per-key uniqueness is the NESTED 'forall ?k: lone ?p: ...' shape that the guard engine currently REJECTS (unsupported_quantifier_form). So either choose a recognizable single-level surface for FunctionalDep, or WI-020 lifts the nested gate for lone-inside-forall. Acceptance: example parses + loads with constraints ENFORCED via the existing GENERAL guard path (works pre-WI-020, just unoptimized); the negative fixture is load-rejected; cargo-test green. Final validation against the optimized discrim-tree path lands with WI-021 / WI-024 (run example)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: PreOpened)
